Data terms (not part of the MIT grant above)

Some folders include data files built from official public sources. The MIT
License covers the code and the compilation work. It does not replace the
terms that apply to the underlying data.

1. CMS files (U.S. government works)

   The RVU, global period, NCCI PTP and MUE tables were built from files
   published by the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services:

   - CY 2026 Physician Fee Schedule Relative Value File, version RVU26D
     (released 08/26/2026), including GPCI values.
     https://www.cms.gov/medicare/payment/fee-schedules/physician/pfs-relative-value-files/rvu26d
   - Medicare NCCI practitioner procedure-to-procedure edits, version 32.3
     revision 0, effective October 1, 2026.
     https://www.cms.gov/medicare/coding-billing/national-correct-coding-initiative-ncci-edits/medicare-ncci-procedure-procedure-ptp-edits
   - Medicare NCCI Practitioner Services Medically Unlikely Edits, effective
     October 1, 2026 (Q4 2026).
     https://www.cms.gov/medicare/coding-billing/national-correct-coding-initiative-ncci-edits/medicare-ncci-medically-unlikely-edits

   Works of the U.S. federal government are not subject to U.S. copyright
   protection (17 U.S.C. § 105). CMS may update or replace these files.
   This repository is a snapshot, not the official source. Always confirm a
   value against the current CMS file before you rely on it.

2. CPT® short descriptors

   The CMS relative value and related files include short descriptors that
   use CPT wording. CPT is a registered trademark of the American Medical
   Association. The AMA holds the copyright in CPT. This repository
   redistributes those short descriptors only as they appear in the CMS
   public files, so the tools can label a code. It is not a substitute for
   a current CPT codebook or an AMA license. If you redistribute this
   data, you are responsible for complying with AMA terms that apply to
   your use.

3. X12 CARC and RARC descriptions

   Official Claim Adjustment Reason Code and Remittance Advice Remark Code
   descriptions in the denial code lookup are copied verbatim from the X12
   code lists, with usage notes omitted. X12 holds the copyright on those
   official descriptions. This table is a convenience copy, not a
   substitute for the current lists:

   - https://x12.org/codes/claim-adjustment-reason-codes
   - https://x12.org/codes/remittance-advice-remark-codes

4. NPPES NPI Registry

   The NPI lookup does not bundle registry data. It queries the public CMS
   NPPES NPI Registry API (version 2.1). Use of that API is subject to
   CMS terms for the registry: https://npiregistry.cms.hhs.gov/api-page
